          "blockId": "BLK_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_4E89B101_CONCEPTS_01_SCALARS_VECTORS_ADDITION",
          "semanticAnchorId": "ANCHOR_SCALARS_VECTORS_ADDITION",
          "title": "1. Scalars, Vectors, and Parallelogram Law",
          "contentMarkdown": "Scalars have magnitude only. Vectors possess magnitude and direction and obey vector addition laws. Parallelogram Law resultant magnitude is $$R = \\\\sqrt{A^2 + B^2 + 2AB\\\\cos\\\\theta}$$ and direction is $$\\tan\\\\alpha = \\\\frac{B\\\\sin\\\\theta}{A + B\\\\cos\\\\theta}$$.",
          "boundAtomicFactIds": [
