          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "BLK_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_4E89B101_CONCEPTS_02_RECTANGULAR_RESOLUTION",
          "semanticAnchorId": "ANCHOR_RECTANGULAR_RESOLUTION",
          "title": "2. Resolution of Vectors into Rectangular Components",
          "contentMarkdown": "A 2D vector resolves into $A_x = A\\\\cos\\\\theta$ and $A_y = A\\\\sin\\\\theta$. The magnitude is $$|A| = \\\\sqrt{A_x^2 + A_y^2}$$ and direction angle is $$\\theta = \\\\arctan(A_y/A_x)$$.",
